# Manim render output. Regenerable via:
#   $MANIM -qh animations/bob_overview.py BOBOverview
# Kept out of git so rendered video never bloats the clone permanently.
media/

# Video. The rendered masters under media/ stay out (they are regenerable and
# each re-render is another full copy), but the four DEPLOYED explainers in
# assets/ are tracked -- the site references them and GitHub Pages has to
# serve something.
#
# Those are web derivatives, not the masters: 30 fps, CRF 26, which is ~66%
# smaller than manim's 1080p60 output and visually identical on slide content
# (RMS difference 1.09/255 on the densest frame). Re-encode with:
#   ffmpeg -i media/videos/<scene>/1080p60/<Scene>.mp4 \
#          -c:v libx264 -crf 26 -preset slow -r 30 \
#          -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart -an assets/<name>.mp4
*.mp4
!assets/*.mp4

# Reference PDFs used while building the animations. Not site content, and
# several are other authors' published papers -- redistributing publisher
# PDFs from a personal domain is a copyright question worth avoiding.
# Nothing on the site links here; the animations cite arXiv numbers instead.
papers/

# One-off exploration scenes: grids of candidate background/accent colours,
# rendered as stills to pick a palette by eye. bg_swatches.py alone is 32
# throwaway Scene classes (BgCyanVivid, BgWVUGoldDeep, ...). They served
# their purpose -- the chosen values now live in the overview scripts -- and
# nothing references them. Kept on disk, out of the repo.
animations/bg_swatches.py
animations/bi_swatches.py

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Windows "downloaded from the internet" markers next to the papers
*:Zone.Identifier
